{"id":"discrete_frechet","title":"Discrete Frechet bottleneck","family":"elastic","definition":"reference","intro_en":"Discrete Frechet comparison minimizes the largest local separation along a monotone traversal. This differs from objectives that add every local mismatch: one difficult pair can determine the bottleneck. Here observations are points on the value axis, with order preserved and no extra time coordinate in the local norm.","intro_zh":"离散 Fréchet 比较最小化单调遍历过程中最大的局部距离。单个困难配对可能决定最终瓶颈。本例将观测视为数值轴上的点，保留其顺序，但局部范数不额外包含时间坐标。","steps_en":["Set the stated local scoring rule, tolerance and boundary conditions.","Keep the larger of the present separation and the smallest predecessor bottleneck.","Trace the selected predecessor operations from the complete-prefix state.","Read the final score with the normalization explicitly stated below."],"steps_zh":["设置明确的局部计分规则、容差与边界条件。","在当前距离和最小前驱瓶颈之间取较大者。","从完整前缀状态沿选定的前驱操作回溯。","按下方明确的归一化约定读取最终分数。"],"formula":"F_ij=max(|x_i-y_j|,min(F_(i-1,j),F_(i,j-1),F_(i-1,j-1)))","caveats_en":["Repeated vertices can make distinct raw vertex lists indistinguishable. Adding time as a coordinate changes the geometry and its scale.","The small arrays are an algorithm illustration, not evidence of retrieval or classification quality."],"caveats_zh":["重复顶点可能使不同原始顶点列表无法区分；加入时间坐标会改变几何与尺度。","这些小数组用于解释计算过程，不构成检索或分类性能证据。"],"sources":[{"label":"Eiter and Mannila (1994): discrete Frechet distance","url":"https://www.kr.tuwien.ac.at/staff/eiter/et-archive/files/cdtr9464.pdf"}],"x":[0.2,0.4,1.1,2.4,3.2,2.5,1.2,0.3,-0.4,-0.1],"y":[0.1,0.3,0.5,1.2,2.6,3.1,2.3,1.1,0.2,-0.3],"input_label":"Deterministic illustrative arrays; no benchmark data","parameters":{"normalization":"none","local_norm":"absolute difference"},"result":{"label":"distance","value":0.20000000000000018,"detail":"The explicit definition and parameters shown on this card."},"frames":[{"phase":0,"caption":"Compare samples to construct the local table","panel":{"kind":"matrix","title":"Local co